## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | BLOCKING | scripts/publish-token-usage.sh | 🚨 blocking sh producer corrupted rows — read r arity never updated for the 6 field python output this pr grows the python counter s output from 4 to 6 fields scripts publish token usage sh 69 — print inp out cr req src model but the consuming read on line 23 still declares 4 variables read dumps every extra field into the last variable so model swallows req src model and sum req source stay at their 0 defaults forever reproduced with this branch s exact counter read bash default ifs legacy ledger — fa tokens input 100 output 50 cacheread 10 model claude x what the fa cli emits today → published row requests 0 source model 0 claude x — the model column is corrupted on every sh published row from day one full ledger — input 1200 output 340 cacheread 9900 requests 42 source reported model claude opus 4 7 → requests 0 source model 42 reported claude opus 4 7 — the new ac2 fields never surface at all this breaks the pr s own ac2 claim both the js producer and the sh producer carry identical semantics for the awf factory teammate path and the corrupted model rides straight into the published data agents tokens json and the board s model column the js producer is unaffected it builds the row in code the sh path has no unit coverage which is how this slipped through fix note — a plain 6 variable read is not enough python s print joins with single spaces so an empty src legacy ledgers until fa grows the field collapses — read r sum in sum out sum cr sum req source model on 100 50 10 0 claude x yields source claude x model verified use an empty field safe hand off instead e g print sentinels src or model or stripped after read or emit one json object and parse with jq r in out please add a counter level test the transport is already exercised end to end by run factorytokenusage json for the js side so the sh arity can t drift again |
| F2 | open | BLOCKING | js/factory/token_usage.js | 🚨 blocking honest retention §3 raised only the js cap — the sh producer still caps at 40 row keep goes 40 → 200 here but the matching jq tail cap in scripts publish token usage sh 119 still reads 40 — this pr touches that file yet leaves the sh side cap untouched every leg published through the awf factory teammate step keeps silently eating history past 40 rows per key — the exact defect §3 the old cap silently ate history — a real leg made 83 turns the file showed 40 exists to fix it also breaks the contract this pr itself documents js factory readme md added in this diff says the shared behavior contract keeps the last 200 per key row keep — the honest cap and §2 claims identical semantics for both producers today js keeps 200 sh keeps 40 readme says 200 — the two producers of one stream diverge and the doc matches neither reality fix raise the sh cap to 200 ideally derive both from one literal — the same single sourcing discipline this pr applies to the path worth a counter level parity test when the sh side test from the read arity finding lands |
| F3 | open | IMPORTANT | js/factory/token_usage.js | ⚠️ important the ac3 consistency test cited as the guard for the single source invariant does not exist this added comment states the canonical path literal is pinned by the ac3 consistency test in js unit tests test factorytokenusage js and the pr description repeats the claim ac3 producer↔tick consistency green no such test exists — grep rn default data path factory tokens asset js unit tests returns nothing each suite test factorytokenusage js test factorystate js test smagent js test aiteammatetokenusagereporter js only pins its own string copies the literals do match today verified js factory token usage js 67 js factorystate js 222 scripts publish token usage sh ai teammate token usage reporter json 20 but nothing fails when one of the four drifts — a future rename on any side passes the whole suite resurrecting exactly the two paths split this pr exists to kill please either add the guard or fix the comment cheap version in test factorystate js which already loads the module assert token usage default data path data factory tokens asset the sh literal can be pinned the same way test ghtokenkeeper js scans glue scripts file read executable line check as shipped the safety property the pr advertises is documented as machine checked when it is not — misleading for the next maintainer |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

