## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F4 | open | BLOCKING | js/factory/token_usage.js | 🚨 blocking the module size ratchet is red on js factory token usage js at this head — 717 lines vs the 714 line pin the rework s docblock rewording ded2bae79 grew js factory token usage js from 714 to 717 physical lines but ci module size baseline json still pins it at 714 — the pin is exceeded and pinned modules may only shrink github workflows quality yml 289 303 crap4js module size baseline ci module size baseline json js the gate measures physical lines including comments — proven first hand by this very head s fix commit eda3cd598 where a comment only docblock rewrap pushed aiteammatetokenusagereporter js to 1925 its 1924 pin and startup fail ed the module size ratchet on the head run 44703077156 that commit fixed the reporter but missed token usage js verified on the current head eda3cd598 clean worktree text git show head ci module size baseline json jq modules js factory token usage js lines 714 functions 44 git show head js factory token usage js wc l 717 every ci run on this branch reds the module size ratchet step of quality yml until this is fixed fix either 1 trim 3 comment lines from the reworded docblocks the 36 8 36 10 and 315 11 317 12 hunks carry the growth or 2 an explicit re pin commit — crap4js module size write baseline raising the pin 714 → 717 with a justification line exactly the pattern c9d83b29c already established in this pr pins move up to the current size option 1 is preferable the growth is pure comment text and eda3cd598 shows the repo prefers rewording back under the pin over raising it |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

